  // The full weight tensor (Cout, Cin, K, K) does not, in general, fit in
  // shared memory (its size grows with Cout), so instead of staging all of
  // it at once we stage COUT_TILE output channels at a time, reusing each
  // chunk across every output position in the tile before moving on.
  // Two buffers are used (double buffering) so that the weight chunk for
  // the NEXT iteration can be loaded from global memory while the CURRENT
  // chunk is still being used for compute, overlapping load latency with
  // useful math instead of stalling at a barrier every iteration.
